# Light text on dark background

Always use **light text on dark backgrounds** in AHCC / AHCCD / AHCCDV (and related UI).

## Rules

- Window/page background: dark (e.g. `#0B1F2A`, `#123D45`).
- Primary text / labels on chrome: light (e.g. `#E8F4F3`).
- Secondary text: muted light (e.g. `#8AA8A6`), never near-white on near-white.
- Buttons, tabs, chips, TextButtons: **dark fill + light foreground** (or transparent/dark + light text). Do **not** use default Windows/Material light tab/button chrome with light text.
- Never leave system-default light TabItem / Button styles on a dark window — override so text stays readable.
- If a control has a light fill, its text must be dark; prefer avoiding light fills in these apps.

## Examples

- Good: Tab `Background="#1A4550"` + `Foreground="#E8F4F3"`
- Bad: Default light tab header + white/light `Foreground` (text disappears)
